## Outcome and conditions

When a member adds contracts during a day, compute existing and new cohorts from their respective reference prices, total daily settlement, incremental and final initial-margin requirement, end-of-day net funding, and conditional temporary funding before settlement. Assume dollars-per-contract q=1, beginning balance exactly the old initial requirement, no withdrawal and all longs in the same specified contract.

Finished-note locations: [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Financial_Markets_Instruments_I/Week_1/Introduction_to_Futures_Seminar_Exercises.md#Problem 5: clearing a larger long position]]; [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Financial_Markets_Instruments_I/Week_1/Margins_and_Marking_to_Market.md#Daily profit and loss, with units]]; [[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Financial_Markets_Instruments_I/Week_1/Margins_and_Marking_to_Market.md#The three margin concepts]].

