## Rubric and independence

The required components are: position_cohort_settlement; new_initial_requirement; net_versus_temporary_funding. Each full check below explicitly elicits and keys every component. Pass requires all its essential reasoning and requested outputs without a critical error. Partial means a correct mechanism but a missing component, unresolved sign/unit, or isolated arithmetic slip. Fail means a critical conceptual error persists or the method cannot establish the result. Unscorable means the response/conditions cannot be interpreted reliably; ask the existing prompt once for clarification, without adding a new assessment. Accept algebraically equivalent expressions, clearly defined opposite cash-flow signs, and plain-language explanations with the same mechanism. An arithmetic slip is partial until independently corrected; it is not automatically a conceptual failure. No numerical score is inferred.

Critical errors: Same reference price for old/new cohorts; deposit counted as profit; one unconditional funding answer when intraday order is unspecified; surplus confused with total P/L.

Acquisition requires two distinct unassisted passes from the explicitly permitted routes O005-I1/O005-I2, O005-I1/O005-D1, O005-I1/O005-D2, O005-I2/O005-D1, O005-I2/O005-D2, O005-D1/O005-D2. I items normally establish acquisition; an unused D item may replace an exposed or failed I item and then cannot later be counted as delayed retention. Each selected full item assesses all listed components, so every route covers them twice. W1, S1, prerequisite diagnostics and the narrow C1 correction are forbidden substitutes. The D bank is finite: never repeat an exposed item to certify fresh learning and never invent changed numbers. If fewer than two unused full items remain, raise a plan_issue for a new prepared bank.

| Component | I1 | I2 | D1 | D2 |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| position_cohort_settlement | required | required | required | required |
| new_initial_requirement | required | required | required | required |
| net_versus_temporary_funding | required | required | required | required |

## Misconceptions and correction

Signs: treating new contracts as held since yesterday; adding margin to profit; equating net funding with entry obligation. Correction: label each cohort's entry/reference, compute G independently, then compare cash with requirement at the specified time. Hint1: new contracts were not open at yesterday's settlement. Hint2: their first change begins at entry. O005-C1 / v1: Two old longs settle50→55, one new enters60 and settles55,q1. What is daily G? Key old+10,new−5,total+5, not+15. Pass cohort bases and sum; partial arithmetic; fail common reference. This narrow check does not supply full funding evidence.

The sign alone is a tentative diagnosis; use the learner's reasoning to establish the confusion. Score the initial response before any hint. Hint 1 points to the named distinction; hint 2 points to the first correct step. After two ineffective hints show the prepared key, then pause if the fresh C1 response still fails. C1 checks the repaired component only and cannot replace a full independent check.

## Immediate and delayed checks

All items are item_version 1 and role full_capability_check. I1/I2 are immediate; D1/D2 are prepared delayed variants. D items may establish delayed success only when unused, unassisted, attempted before recap, at least 24 elapsed hours after acquisition and the most recent relevant solution/teaching exposure, with intervening exposure recorded. Early D attempts may be immediate checks but are not delayed evidence. Each delayed success is separate from initial acquisition. Numerical changes are parallel variants; a changed buyer/seller context is bounded near transfer, never proof of broad transfer.

### O005-I1

**Prompt:** Hypothetical eight old longs settled200, two new entered215, all settle210; margin40 per contract,q1. Beginning account exactly old initial. Compute cohort and total settlement, incremental/final margin, end-of-day additional funding/surplus, and temporary cash if new margin is due before settlement. Explain why the two funding amounts can differ and reconcile account if the entry deposit is actually made.

**Key and essential rubric:** Old8×10=+80; new2×(−5)=−10; Gtotal+70. Beginning320, incremental80, final400. Unfunded ending390, net extra10, no surplus. Entry temporary80 if due first; after that deposit ending470, excess70; P/L470−400=70. Difference arises timing and gains available only later; new obligation80 remains distinct from net cash10. All three components required.

### O005-I2

**Prompt:** Hypothetical six old longs settled1000, four new entered1020, final1010; margin50/contract,q1. Starting balance old initial only. Give old/new/net settlement, incremental/final requirement, net end funding/excess and entry-before-settlement funding; reconcile the account after that entry deposit and explain the timing.

**Key and essential rubric:** Old+60,new−40,net+20. Beginning300,increment200,final500. Without entry deposit end320→net extra180,excess0. If new200 due before settlement, temporary200; then end520,excess20 and P/L520−500=20. Different price bases/entry obligation and daily gains explain net180 vs temporary200. All three components required.

### O005-D1

**Prompt:** Hypothetical ten old longs settled50, five new entered54, final53, margin10/contract,q1. Compute cohort/net P/L, new/final margin, end-of-day funding/excess and entry-time funding conditional on due-before-settlement, then reconcile the funded account.

**Key and essential rubric:** Old+30,new−5,total+25. Beginning100,increment50,final150. Without funding end125→net extra25,excess0. Entry temporary50; funded end175,excess25; P/L175−150=25. New cohort starts at54; obligation50 is independent of net25, timing conditional. All three components required.

### O005-D2

**Prompt:** Hypothetical five old longs settled300, one new entered340, final330, margin100/contract,q1. Calculate cohort/net settlement, incremental/final requirement, end-day extra/excess and conditional entry funding. Reconcile ending account if new margin is paid first and explain why favorable net settlement does not mean the new initial requirement vanishes.

**Key and essential rubric:** Old+150,new−10,total+140. Beginning500,increment100,final600. Without entry funding end640→net extra0,excess40. If100 due before settlement temporary100,then end740/excess140, P/L740−600=140. Obligation100 still exists; net later gains cover it under netting. All three components required.

## Advance, revisit, pause, and escalate

